  "result": "Perfect! All 147 tests pass. I've successfully added a payments module to handle invoice payments:\n\n**`src/payments.js` provides:**\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an invoice\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added to invoice.payments array\n   - Errors:\n     - `NOT_ISSUED`: Invoice must be 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (not draft or paid)\n     - `AMOUNT_INVALID`: Amount must be a positive integer\n     - `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment exceeds remaining balance\n   - Updates invoice status:\n     - `'partially_paid'` when payment partially covers the balance\n     - `'paid'` when total payments cover the full invoice total\n   - Never mutates original invoice\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Calculates amount still owed\n   - Returns `invoiceTotal - sumOfPayments`\n   - Clamps at 0 minimum\n   - Handles missing payments array gracefully\n\n3. **New error codes added to errors.js:**\n   - `NOT_ISSUED`: Can't record payments on non-issued invoices\n   - `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment exceeds the amount still owed\n\n**Test coverage includes:**\n- Recording single and multiple payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error validation (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, OVERPAYMENT)\n- Balance calculations with various payment scenarios\n- Mutation safety\n\nThe payment system properly tracks invoice payment status and enforces business rules around overpayments and invalid states. \u2714",
